  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "For $\\triangle ABC$ we are given that $a=6$, $\\angle A=30^\\circ$ and $\\angle B=45^\\circ$. Find the area of the triangle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$(9\\sqrt{3}+9)$ square units.\n\nFind $AC$ using the sine rule, then drop a perpendicular from $C$ to $AB$ and use half the base times the height.",
      "worked": "Using the sine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{b}{\\sin45^\\circ}&=\\frac{6}{\\sin30^\\circ}\\\\\nb&=\\frac{6\\sin45^\\circ}{\\sin30^\\circ}\\\\\nb&=6\\sqrt2.\n\\end{align*}$$\nLet $D$ be the foot of the perpendicular from $C$ to $AB$. Since $A=30^\\circ$ and $B=45^\\circ$, $D$ lies between $A$ and $B$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\nCD&=AC\\sin30^\\circ=3\\sqrt2\\\\\nAD&=AC\\cos30^\\circ=3\\sqrt6\\\\\nBD&=CD=3\\sqrt2\\\\\nAB&=AD+BD=3\\sqrt6+3\\sqrt2.\n\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\operatorname{area}(\\triangle ABC)&=\\frac12 AB\\cdot CD\\\\\n&=\\frac12(3\\sqrt6+3\\sqrt2)(3\\sqrt2)\\\\\n&=9\\sqrt3+9.\n\\end{align*}$$\nThe area is $(9\\sqrt3+9)$ square units.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
